# VPM-2 — Vulnerabilities scanned and remediated

**Vanta control:** VPM-2
**Frameworks:** SOC 2 CC 2.1, CC 4.1 (+4 more)
**Status at start:** 15/17 tests passing — 2 failing
**Investigated:** 2026-04-30

---

## Situation

### Control intent (Vanta VPM-2 standard)
- Recurring (typically quarterly) vulnerability scans of production / external-facing systems
- Critical/high findings tracked to remediation within SLA
- Documented vulnerability-management process

### Current scanning posture at Normain
Source: `Automated Security Testing Procedure` v1.0, CTO-owned, effective 2025-07-04 (Drive doc `1qHPB6W1lilVFo_gazrr6BOQA1_FG3U7gXjwBDzQ3mf4`).

| Layer | Tool | Cadence |
|---|---|---|
| SAST | GitHub CodeQL | every PR |
| SCA | Dependabot | daily + on PR |
| DAST | OWASP ZAP Baseline (`analysis-dast.yml`) | weekly Sun 02:00 UTC, prod |
| Container | Gryve | on image build |
| Pen test | External (`Normain Penetration Test Report 20250516.pdf`) | annual |
| Firewall/network | `Firewall and Network Security Assessment - 25-08-25` | one-off |

Remediation SLA per ASTP: critical issues ≤ 30 days; MTTR tracked monthly via GitHub Security → Overview.

### Gap vs VPM-2
No **host-based / OS-level** vulnerability scanner on running production hosts. ASTP covers code, deps, container image at build time, and web-app DAST — not the running OS surface. Production runs on Azure (`deploy.azure.yml`); Defender for Cloud / Microsoft Defender Vulnerability Management is the natural fit but no evidence found of it being enabled or quarterly reports captured into Vanta.

### 2 failing tests — could not confirm directly
**Blocker:** Vanta UI is gated behind login. `slay tasks browser` requires the task tab to be active in slay (returns "Browser panel did not open within timeout. Is the task tab active?"). chrome-devtools MCP opens an isolated, unauthenticated session.

Inferred from VPM-2's standard test set (verify in UI before acting):
1. **Quarterly host-based vulnerability scan completed** — needs scan-report evidence uploaded
2. **Critical/high vulnerabilities remediated within SLA** — Vanta auto-checks GitHub Security alerts; if open Critical/High exist past SLA, this fails. Likely tied to siblings #11 (Critical) and #29 (High).

